      "description": "Original instrumental miniature for a handmade shadow rehearsal theatre. A timid paper dancer follows a small light, discovers a brave leap, joins a mirrored duet, then bows warmly. No vocals, speech, humming or choir.",
      "instrumental": true,
      "title": "A Little Light Rehearsal",
      "lyrics": "[instrumental]",
      "global_meta": "Genre: playful acoustic chamber miniature, tactile handmade theatre. BPM: 100. Key: D major. Duration target: 35 seconds, continuous instrumental, no long introduction. Mood progression: first 0-8 seconds tentative and curious; 8-16 seconds courage and a light upward leap; 16-24 seconds flowing mirrored duet; 24-32 seconds warm theatrical bow; 32-35 seconds natural ending and gentle decay. Intimate acoustic stereo, natural dynamics, clear melodic motif, gentle low end.",
      "vocals": "Instrumental only. No vocals, spoken words, humming, choir, vocal chops or sung melody.",
      "arrangement": "Begin immediately with a sparse warm felt-piano motif and quiet pizzicato strings, leaving breathing room for the timid dancer. In the second 8-second section the motif climbs as light wooden percussion and marimba answer it, a short upward flourish accompanies the leap. In the third section two complementary piano and plucked-string phrases answer one another like mirrored dancers, supported by soft brushed rhythm. In the fourth section bring the same motif home with warm strings and a restrained satisfying final chord. Let the last three seconds decay naturally. Memorable, lightly mischievous and tender, acoustic instruments, no electronic beeps, no aggressive bass, no cinematic bombast, no vocals."
    },
